post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
MusicIndex live publisher was installed.

Quick Mixxx setup:
  setup-mixxx-musicindex

Temporary test setup for the current login session:
  setup-mixxx-musicindex --temporary

The publisher uses a fixed dead block while idle or playing non-V4V audio
(ADR 0005). No configuration changes it.

The setup command provisions a live item, writes the one-time broadcaster token,
generates musicindex-live-publisher@mixxx.service and mixxx-now-playing.service,
then starts the user services.

Upgrade: run "setup-mixxx-musicindex --units-only" to write the two units again.
It changes no config and no token, and it sends no relay request.

MIDI connector (ADR 0006):
  The package installs the V4V MIDI card files. The V4V card exists after the
  next reboot. This install does not load the kernel module.
  If this computer already uses snd-virmidi, merge the options before you
  reboot. The configuration runbook, section "MIDI Connector", gives the steps.

  After the reboot, start Mixxx. In Mixxx, open Preferences, Controllers,
  VirMIDI 31-0. Select the mapping "MusicIndex V4V Connector" and enable the
  controller.

Only run one mixxx-now-playing service. Future non-Mixxx producers can use
separate musicindex-live-publisher@<instance>.service instances.

Docs:
  /usr/share/doc/musicindex-live-publisher/musicindex-live-publisher-arch-package.md
  /usr/share/doc/musicindex-live-publisher/musicindex-live-publisher-configuration.md
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install "$1"
}
